Template: pubsec-rspamd/api-url
Type: string
Default: http://127.0.0.1:8081
Description: URL of the pubsecd REST API:
 pubsec-rspamd reports spam senders seen by Rspamd to a pubsecd instance and
 reads the active list back from it. Enter the address of the internal REST
 API, which is the [api] bind address in the pubsecd configuration.

Template: pubsec-rspamd/push-token
Type: password
Description: pubsecd API token with the "push" scope:
 This token is used to report spam senders. Create it in pubsec-tui on the
 Tokens tab; the secret is shown only once.
 .
 Leave empty to configure the token by hand later. Until the tokens are set,
 the service is not started and Rspamd is not set up to use it.

Template: pubsec-rspamd/read-token
Type: password
Description: pubsecd API token with the "read" scope:
 This token is used to fetch the active list that Rspamd scores messages
 with. Its max_tlp setting limits which entries are handed out.
 .
 Leave empty to configure the token by hand later.

Template: pubsec-rspamd/report
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Report senders of spam to pubsecd?
 A plugin in Rspamd sends the result of each scanned message to
 pubsec-rspamd. IPs that keep sending messages with a high spam score are
 published to pubsecd as observations (TLP:GREEN).
 .
 Authenticated users are never reported. Scores added by the pubsecd active
 list itself are not counted.

Template: pubsec-rspamd/report-domains
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Also report envelope-from domains of spam?
 The domain of the SMTP envelope sender of spam messages is reported as well
 (TLP:GREEN), but only if SPF authorised the sending IP for it. Freemail and
 disposable providers and the bounce domains of common mail service providers
 are skipped.

Template: pubsec-rspamd/ignore-networks
Type: string
Default:
Description: Networks that must never be reported:
 IP addresses or prefixes of your own relays, backup MX and forwarders,
 separated by spaces or commas, e.g. "192.0.2.10, 2001:db8::/48".
 .
 Entries of the pubsecd allowlist are honoured as well.

Template: pubsec-rspamd/own-domains
Type: string
Default:
Description: Own domains that must never be reported:
 Domains whose envelope-from must never be reported, e.g. the domains you send
 mail for, separated by spaces or commas. Subdomains are covered as well.

Template: pubsec-rspamd/use-maps
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Score messages with the pubsecd active list?
 pubsec-rspamd can serve the pubsecd active list to Rspamd's multimap module,
 so that sending IPs, URL hosts and sender domains reported by your peers add
 to the spam score (symbols PUBSEC_BAD_*). The rules are installed as
 /etc/rspamd/local.d/pubsec_multimap.inc.

Template: pubsec-rspamd/multimap-note
Type: note
Description: Include the pubsec multimap rules in multimap.conf
 /etc/rspamd/local.d/multimap.conf already exists, so it was not changed.
 Add this line to it to activate the pubsec rules:
 .
  .include(try=true) "$LOCAL_CONFDIR/local.d/pubsec_multimap.inc"
 .
 Then reload Rspamd.

Template: pubsec-rspamd/multimap-remove-note
Type: note
Description: Remove the pubsec multimap rules from multimap.conf
 /etc/rspamd/local.d/multimap.conf includes the pubsec multimap rules, but
 the active list is no longer served, so Rspamd cannot load the maps. Remove
 this line from it:
 .
  .include(try=true) "$LOCAL_CONFDIR/local.d/pubsec_multimap.inc"
 .
 Then reload Rspamd.
